{"id":"0a1a27e4a79efc6c0654fba093445b23d7a960d7","axis":"silent","repo":"envoyproxy/envoy","sha":"0a1a27e4a79efc6c0654fba093445b23d7a960d7","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"changelogs/current/bug_fixes/server__ocsp-response-expiration-gauge.rst","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@","+Fixed the ``server.seconds_until_first_ocsp_response_expiring`` statistic, which kept reporting the","+expiration of the last OCSP response once no TLS context had an OCSP response, for example after a","+certificate with an OCSP staple was replaced by one without a staple or its listener was removed. It","+now drops to 0, its value before the first OCSP response."],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"changelogs/current/new_features/dynamic_modules__add-tls-certificate-selector-support.rst","lines":["@@ -6,4 +6,8 @@ select one. With :ref:`allow_dynamic_certificates"," <envoy_v3_api_field_extensions.transport_sockets.tls.cert_selectors.dynamic_modules.v3.DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelector.allow_dynamic_certificates>`"," set, the module can also select certificates that it provides at runtime, and a handshake can wait"," for one that is not provided yet. Modules can schedule work on the main thread and record metrics.","-This works for both downstream and upstream TLS contexts.","+This works for both downstream and upstream TLS contexts. The dynamic certificates that are served","+are listed by the ``/certs`` admin endpoint and count in the","+``server.days_until_first_cert_expiring`` and ``server.seconds_until_first_ocsp_response_expiring``","+statistics, and the selector emits","+:ref:`statistics <config_tls_certificate_selectors_dynamic_modules>` about them."],"additions":5,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/root/configuration/observability/statistics.rst","lines":["@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ Server related statistics are rooted at *server.* with following statistics:","   total_connections, Gauge, Total connections of both new and old Envoy processes","   version, Gauge, Integer represented version number based on SCM revision or :ref:`stats_server_version_override <envoy_v3_api_field_config.bootstrap.v3.Bootstrap.stats_server_version_override>` if set.","   days_until_first_cert_expiring, Gauge, Number of days until the next certificate being managed will expire","-  seconds_until_first_ocsp_response_expiring, Gauge, Number of seconds until the next OCSP response being managed will expire","+  seconds_until_first_ocsp_response_expiring, Gauge, \"Number of seconds until the next OCSP response being managed will expire, or 0 when no OCSP response is managed\"","   hot_restart_epoch, Gauge, Current hot restart epoch -- an integer passed via command line flag ``--restart-epoch`` usually indicating generation.","   hot_restart_generation, Gauge, Current hot restart generation -- like hot_restart_epoch but computed automatically by incrementing from parent.","   hot_restart_udp_forwarding_datagrams, Counter, Datagrams of UDP packets this (parent) instance forwarded to its hot restart child while draining."],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/root/configuration/security/dynamic_modules_tls_certificate_selector.rst","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@","+.. _config_tls_certificate_selectors_dynamic_modules:","+","+Dynamic modules TLS certificate selector","+========================================","+","+The :ref:`DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelector","+<envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.transport_sockets.tls.cert_selectors.dynamic_modules.v3.DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelector>`","+configuration specifies a :ref:`custom TLS certificate selector","+<envoy_v3_api_field_extensions.transport_sockets.tls.v3.CommonTlsContext.custom_tls_certificate_selector>`","+backed by a :ref:`dynamic module <arch_overview_dynamic_modules>`. For each handshake the module","+selects one of the configured certificates, lets Envoy select one, or selects a dynamic certificate","+that it provides at runtime.","+","+* :ref:`v3 API reference <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.transport_sockets.tls.cert_selectors.dynamic_modules.v3.DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelector>`","+","+Once the TLS context is ready to serve handshakes, its dynamic certificates are listed by the","+:ref:`/certs <operations_admin_interface_certs>` admin endpoint, without the trusted certificates that","+the TLS context lists itself, and they count in the ``server.days_until_first_cert_expiring`` and","+``server.seconds_until_first_ocsp_response_expiring`` statistics.","+","+Statistics","+----------","+","+With :ref:`allow_dynamic_certificates","+<envoy_v3_api_field_extensions.transport_sockets.tls.cert_selectors.dynamic_modules.v3.DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelector.allow_dynamic_certificates>`","+set, the selector emits the following statistics. For downstream listeners, they are in the","+*listener.<address>.dynamic_certificates.* namespace, or *listener.<stat_prefix>.dynamic_certificates.*","+if :ref:`stat_prefix <envoy_v3_api_field_config.listener.v3.Listener.stat_prefix>` is non-empty. For","+filter chains from the Filter Chain Discovery Service (FCDS), they are in the *dynamic_certificates.*","+namespace. For upstream clusters, they are in the *cluster.<name>.dynamic_certificates.* namespace,","+or *cluster.<alt_stat_name>.dynamic_certificates.* if :ref:`alt_stat_name","+<envoy_v3_api_field_config.cluster.v3.Cluster.alt_stat_name>` is non-empty.","+","+.. csv-table::","+  :header: Name, Type, Description","+  :widths: 1, 1, 2","+","+  requested, Counter, Total number of dynamic certificate requests to the module","+  provided, Counter, Total number of dynamic certificates that the module provided and Envoy accepted","+  rejected, Counter, Total number of dynamic certificates that the module provided and Envoy rejected","+  removed, Counter, Total number of dynamic certificates removed by the module or because they failed with an updated TLS context","+  active, Gauge, Number of dynamic certificates that are served","+  pending, Gauge, Number of dynamic certificate requests that wait for the module"],"additions":43,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/root/configuration/security/security.rst","lines":["@@ -5,3 +5,4 @@ Security","   :maxdepth: 2"," ","   secret","+  dynamic_modules_tls_certificate_selector"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/root/intro/arch_overview/advanced/dynamic_modules.rst","lines":["@@ -33,7 +33,8 @@ Currently, dynamic modules are supported at the following extension points:"," * As an :ref:`HTTP/1 header formatter <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.http.header_formatters.dynamic_modules.v3.DynamicModuleHeaderFormatter>`."," * As an :ref:`HTTP matching data input <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.matching.http.dynamic_modules.v3.HttpDynamicModuleMatchInput>`."," * As an :ref:`input matcher <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.matching.input_matchers.dynamic_modules.v3.DynamicModuleMatcher>`.","-* As a :ref:`TLS certificate selector <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.transport_sockets.tls.cert_selectors.dynamic_modules.v3.DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelector>`.","+* As a :ref:`TLS certificate selector <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.transport_sockets.tls.cert_selectors.dynamic_modules.v3.DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelector>`","+  (:ref:`configuration <config_tls_certificate_selectors_dynamic_modules>`)."," * As a :ref:`TLS certificate validator <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.transport_sockets.tls.cert_validator.dynamic_modules.v3.DynamicModuleCertValidatorConfig>`."," * As a :ref:`TLS handshaker <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.transport_sockets.tls.handshakers.dynamic_modules.v3.DynamicModuleTlsHandshaker>`."," * As a :ref:`transport socket <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.transport_sockets.dynamic_modules.v3.DynamicModuleTransportSocket>`."],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"envoy/ssl/context_manager.h","lines":["@@ -65,6 +65,13 @@ class ContextManager {","    */","   virtual std::optional<uint64_t> secondsUntilFirstOcspResponseExpires() const PURE;"," ","+  /**","+   * Add an ssl context that is built outside of the manager. The manager holds it and includes it","+   * in iterateContexts() and the expiration queries until removeContext() removes it. Must be","+   * called on the main thread, once for each context. A null context is ignored.","+   */","+  virtual void addContext(const Envoy::Ssl::ContextSharedPtr& context) PURE;","+","   /**","    * Remove an existing ssl context.","    */"],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/common/tls/context_manager_impl.cc","lines":["@@ -92,6 +92,14 @@ void ContextManagerImpl::iterateContexts(std::function<void(const Envoy::Ssl::Co","   }"," }"," ","+void ContextManagerImpl::addContext(const Envoy::Ssl::ContextSharedPtr& context) {","+  ASSERT_IS_MAIN_OR_TEST_THREAD();","+  if (context != nullptr) {","+    const bool inserted = contexts_.insert(context).second;","+    ASSERT(inserted);","+  }","+}","+"," void ContextManagerImpl::removeContext(const Envoy::Ssl::ContextSharedPtr& old_context) {","   if (old_context != nullptr) {","     auto erased = contexts_.erase(old_context);"],"additions":8,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/common/tls/context_manager_impl.h","lines":["@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@ class ContextManagerImpl final : public Envoy::Ssl::ContextManager {","   Ssl::PrivateKeyMethodManager& privateKeyMethodManager() override {","     return private_key_method_manager_;","   };","+  void addContext(const Envoy::Ssl::ContextSharedPtr& context) override;","   void removeContext(const Envoy::Ssl::ContextSharedPtr& old_context) override;"," "," private:"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/cert_selectors/common/async_context.h","lines":["@@ -22,8 +22,9 @@ namespace Tls {"," namespace CertificateSelectors {"," "," class AsyncContext;","+using AsyncContextSharedPtr = std::shared_ptr<AsyncContext>;"," using AsyncContextConstSharedPtr = std::shared_ptr<const AsyncContext>;","-using AsyncContextFactory = absl::AnyInvocable<AsyncContextConstSharedPtr(","+using AsyncContextFactory = absl::AnyInvocable<AsyncContextSharedPtr(","     Stats::Scope&, Server::Configuration::ServerFactoryContext&, const Ssl::TlsCertificateConfig&,","     absl::Status&)>;"," "],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/cert_selectors/dynamic_modules/BUILD","lines":["@@ -23,8 +23,11 @@ envoy_cc_library(","         \"//envoy/network:transport_socket_interface\",","         \"//envoy/server:factory_context_interface\",","         \"//envoy/ssl:context_config_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/ssl:context_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/ssl:context_manager_interface\",","         \"//envoy/ssl:handshaker_interface\",","         \"//envoy/stats:stats_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/stats:stats_macros\",","         \"//envoy/thread_local:thread_local_interface\",","         \"//source/common/common:assert_lib\",","         \"//source/common/common:minimal_logger_lib\",","@@ -35,6 +38,7 @@ envoy_cc_library(","         \"//source/common/stats:utility_lib\",","         \"//source/common/tls:context_lib\",","         \"//source/common/tls:server_context_lib\",","+        \"//source/common/tls:utility_lib\",","         \"//source/extensions/dynamic_modules:abi_context_accessors_lib\",","         \"//source/extensions/dynamic_modules:abi_impl\",","         \"//source/extensions/dynamic_modules:dynamic_modules_lib\","],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/cert_selectors/dynamic_modules/tls_certificate_selector.cc","lines":["@@ -1,10 +1,13 @@"," #include \"source/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/cert_selectors/dynamic_modules/tls_certificate_selector.h\""," ","+#include <algorithm>","+"," #include \"envoy/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/cert.pb.h\""," "," #include \"source/common/common/thread.h\""," #include \"source/common/tls/default_tls_certificate_selector.h\""," #include \"source/common/tls/server_context_impl.h\"","+#include \"source/common/tls/utility.h\""," #include \"source/server/generic_factory_context.h\""," "," #include \"absl/strings/str_cat.h\"","@@ -43,6 +46,34 @@ bool validationContextReady(const Ssl::ContextConfig& tls_config) {","          tls_config.certificateValidationContext() != nullptr;"," }"," ","+// Reports a dynamic certificate to the context manager without the trusted certificates, which the","+// TLS context of the selector reports once for all of its dynamic certificates.","+class DynamicCertificateView : public Ssl::Context {","+public:","+  DynamicCertificateView(AsyncContextConstSharedPtr context, TimeSource& time_source)","+      : context_(std::move(context)),","+        ssl_context_(dynamic_cast<const Ssl::Context*>(context_.get())), time_source_(time_source) {","+    ASSERT(ssl_context_ != nullptr);","+  }","+","+  // Ssl::Context","+  std::optional<uint32_t> daysUntilFirstCertExpires() const override {","+    return Utility::getDaysUntilExpiration(context_->tlsContext().cert_chain_.get(), time_source_);","+  }","+  std::vector<Ssl::CertificateDetailsPtr> getCaCertInformation() const override { return {}; }","+  std::vector<Ssl::CertificateDetailsPtr> getCertChainInformation() const override {","+    return ssl_context_->getCertChainInformation();","+  }","+  std::optional<uint64_t> secondsUntilFirstOcspResponseExpires() const override {","+    return ssl_context_->secondsUntilFirstOcspResponseExpires();","+  }","+","+private:","+  const AsyncContextConstSharedPtr context_;","+  const Ssl::Context* const ssl_context_;","+  TimeSource& time_source_;","+};","+"," } // namespace"," "," void DynamicCertificateHandle::notify(AsyncContextConstSharedPtr context) {","@@ -67,12 +98,19 @@ DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorCo","     AsyncContextFactory dynamic_context_factory)","     : main_thread_dispatcher_(factory_context.serverFactoryContext().mainThreadDispatcher()),","       dynamic_module_(std::move(dynamic_module)),","-      server_context_(factory_context.serverFactoryContext()), tls_config_(&tls_config),","+      server_context_(factory_context.serverFactoryContext()),","+      context_manager_(server_context_.sslContextManager()), tls_config_(&tls_config),","       dynamic_context_factory_(std::move(dynamic_context_factory)),","       context_scope_(factory_context.scope().createScope(\"\")),","       stats_scope_(server_context_.scope().createScope(absl::StrCat(metrics_namespace, \".\"))),","       metrics_(*stats_scope_) {","   if (dynamic_context_factory_ != nullptr) {","+    // The socket factory is created right after the configuration, and installs a TLS context built","+    // from it if it is ready.","+    tls_context_installed_ = tls_config.isReady();","+    stats_ = std::make_unique<DynamicCertificateStats>(DynamicCertificateStats{","+        ALL_DYNAMIC_CERTIFICATE_STATS(POOL_COUNTER_PREFIX(*context_scope_, \"dynamic_certificates\"),","+                                      POOL_GAUGE_PREFIX(*context_scope_, \"dynamic_certificates\"))});","     thread_local_certificates_ =","         ThreadLocal::TypedSlot<ThreadLocalCertificates>::makeUnique(server_context_.threadLocal());","     thread_local_certificates_->set(","@@ -84,6 +122,12 @@ DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::~DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorC","   if (in_module_config_ != nullptr) {","     on_config_destroy_(in_module_config_);","   }","+  // Requests still waiting for the module end with the configuration.","+  if (stats_ != nullptr) {","+    stats_->pending_.sub(std::count_if(","+        dynamic_certificates_.begin(), dynamic_certificates_.end(),","+        [](const auto& entry) { return !entry.second.certificate_config.has_value(); }));","+  }"," }"," "," bool DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::setCertificate(absl::string_view name,","@@ -105,6 +149,7 @@ bool DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::setCertificate(absl::string_view","   if (tls_config_ == nullptr) {","     ENVOY_LOG(debug, \"dynamic module set TLS certificate '{}', but its TLS context is removed\",","               name);","+    stats_->rejected_.inc();","     failRequestedCertificate(name);","     return false;","   }","@@ -113,9 +158,11 @@ bool DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::setCertificate(absl::string_view","   if (!status.ok()) {","     ENVOY_LOG(warn, \"dynamic module set an invalid TLS certificate '{}': {}\", name,","               status.message());","+    stats_->rejected_.inc();","     failRequestedCertificate(name);","     return false;","   }","+  stats_->provided_.inc();","   return true;"," }"," ","@@ -144,17 +191,28 @@ absl::Status DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::addCertificate(","   RETURN_IF_NOT_OK_REF(certificate_config.status());","   // onConfigUpdate() builds the certificate once the validation context arrives.","   if (!validationContextReady(*tls_config_)) {","-    dynamic_certificates_[name].certificate_config.emplace(*std::move(certificate_config));","+    storeProvidedCertificate(name, *std::move(certificate_config));","     return absl::OkStatus();","   }","   auto context = buildContext(*certificate_config);","   RETURN_IF_NOT_OK_REF(context.status());","-  DynamicCertificate& certificate = dynamic_certificates_[name];","-  certificate.certificate_config.emplace(*std::move(certificate_config));","+  DynamicCertificate& certificate = storeProvidedCertificate(name, *std::move(certificate_config));","   activateCertificate(name, certificate, *std::move(context));","   return absl::OkStatus();"," }"," ","+DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::DynamicCertificate&","+DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::storeProvidedCertificate(","+    const std::string& name, Ssl::TlsCertificateConfigImpl&& certificate_config) {","+  const auto [it, inserted] = dynamic_certificates_.try_emplace(name);","+  DynamicCertificate& certificate = it->second;","+  if (!inserted && !certificate.certificate_config.has_value()) {","+    stats_->pending_.dec();","+  }","+  certificate.certificate_config.emplace(std::move(certificate_config));","+  return certificate;","+}","+"," void DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::removeCertificate(absl::string_view name) {","   if (!Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","     IS_ENVOY_BUG(\"envoy_dynamic_module_callback_tls_certificate_selector_config_remove_certificate \"","@@ -170,6 +228,12 @@ void DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::removeCertificate(absl::string_v","   if (it->second.context != nullptr) {","     updateWorkers(it->first, nullptr);","   }","+  if (it->second.certificate_config.has_value()) {","+    stats_->removed_.inc();","+  } else {","+    stats_->pending_.dec();","+  }","+  replaceManagedContext(it->second, nullptr);","   dynamic_certificates_.erase(it);","   for (const auto& weak_handle : waiting_handles) {","     if (const auto handle = weak_handle.lock(); handle != nullptr) {","@@ -180,6 +244,14 @@ void DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::removeCertificate(absl::string_v"," "," void DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::onConfigUpdate() {","   ASSERT_IS_MAIN_OR_TEST_THREAD();","+  // The socket factory installed a TLS context built from the updated configuration before this","+  // call, or none if the configuration is not ready.","+  tls_context_installed_ = tls_config_->isReady();","+  if (!tls_context_installed_) {","+    for (auto& [_, certificate] : dynamic_certificates_) {","+      replaceManagedContext(certificate, nullptr);","+    }","+  }","   if (!validationContextReady(*tls_config_)) {","     return;","   }","@@ -206,6 +278,10 @@ void DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::onConfigUpdate() {"," "," void DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::detachTlsConfig() {","   ASSERT_IS_MAIN_OR_TEST_THREAD();","+  // The context manager is main thread state, and the configuration may be destroyed on a worker.","+  for (auto& [_, certificate] : dynamic_certificates_) {","+    replaceManagedContext(certificate, nullptr);","+  }","   tls_config_ = nullptr;","   dynamic_context_factory_ = nullptr;"," }","@@ -273,22 +349,34 @@ void DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::requestCertificate(","   certificate.waiting_handles.push_back(handle);","   if (inserted) {","     ENVOY_LOG(debug, \"requesting TLS certificate '{}' from the dynamic module\", name);","+    stats_->requested_.inc();","+    stats_->pending_.inc();","     // The hook can provide or remove the certificate, so the entry is not used after it returns.","     on_certificate_requested_(this, in_module_config_, {name.data(), name.size()});","   }"," }"," ","-absl::StatusOr<AsyncContextConstSharedPtr> DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::buildContext(","+absl::StatusOr<AsyncContextSharedPtr> DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::buildContext(","     const Ssl::TlsCertificateConfig& certificate_config) {","   absl::Status creation_status = absl::OkStatus();","-  AsyncContextConstSharedPtr context = dynamic_context_factory_(","-      *context_scope_, server_context_, certificate_config, creation_status);","+  AsyncContextSharedPtr context = dynamic_context_factory_(*context_scope_, server_context_,","+                                                           certificate_config, creation_status);","   RETURN_IF_NOT_OK(creation_status);","   return context;"," }"," ","-void DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::activateCertificate(","-    const std::string& name, DynamicCertificate& certificate, AsyncContextConstSharedPtr context) {","+void DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::activateCertificate(const std::string& name,","+                                                                    DynamicCertificate& certificate,","+                                                                    AsyncContextSharedPtr context) {","+  // Only a certificate that an installed TLS context can serve is reported. onConfigUpdate()","+  // activates the certificate again once a TLS context is installed, and a handshaker that","+  // provides the certificates builds the context without one.","+  Ssl::ContextSharedPtr managed_context;","+  if (tls_context_installed_ && context->tlsContext().cert_chain_ != nullptr) {","+    managed_context =","+        std::make_shared<DynamicCertificateView>(context, server_context_.timeSource());","+  }","+  replaceManagedContext(certificate, std::move(managed_context));","   certificate.context = context;","   updateWorkers(name, context);","   for (const auto& weak_handle : std::exchange(certificate.waiting_handles, {})) {","@@ -298,6 +386,19 @@ void DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::activateCertificate(","   }"," }"," ","+void DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::replaceManagedContext(","+    DynamicCertificate& certificate, Ssl::ContextSharedPtr&& context) {","+  if (certificate.managed_context != nullptr) {","+    context_manager_.removeContext(certificate.managed_context);","+    stats_->active_.dec();","+  }","+  certificate.managed_context = std::move(context);","+  if (certificate.managed_context != nullptr) {","+    context_manager_.addContext(certificate.managed_context);","+    stats_->active_.inc();","+  }","+}","+"," void DynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig::updateWorkers(const std::string& name,","                                                               AsyncContextConstSharedPtr context) {","   // The module can still change certificates from its destroy hooks after threading shuts down.","@@ -371,6 +472,8 @@ newDynamicModuleTlsCertificateSelectorConfig(","   config->in_module_config_ = on_config_new.value()(static_cast<void*>(config.get()), name_buffer,","                                                     config_buffer, is_upstream);","   if (config->in_module_config_ == nullptr) {","+    // The module may have provided dynamic certificates before it failed.","+    config->detachTlsConfig();","     return absl::InvalidArgumentError(","         \"Failed to initialize dynamic module TLS certificate selector config\");","   }"],"additions":112,"deletions":9,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/cert_selectors/dynamic_modules/tls_certificate_selector.h","lines":["@@ -9,9 +9,12 @@"," #include \"envoy/common/optref.h\""," #include \"envoy/event/dispatcher.h\""," #include \"envoy/server/factory_context.h\"","+#include \"envoy/ssl/context.h\""," #include \"envoy/ssl/context_config.h\"","+#include \"envoy/ssl/context_manager.h\""," #include \"envoy/ssl/handshaker.h\""," #include \"envoy/stats/scope.h\"","+#include \"envoy/stats/stats_macros.h\""," #include \"envoy/thread_local/thread_local.h\""," "," #include \"source/common/common/assert.h\"","@@ -54,6 +57,19 @@ using OnTlsCertificateSelectorConfigScheduledType ="," // This can be overridden via the ``metrics_namespace`` field in ``DynamicModuleConfig``."," constexpr absl::string_view DefaultMetricsNamespace = \"dynamicmodulescustom\";"," ","+#define ALL_DYNAMIC_CERTIFICATE_STATS(COUNTER, GAUGE)                                              \\","+  COUNTER(provided)                                                                                \\","+  COUNTER(rejected)                                                                                \\","+  COUNTER(removed)                                                                                 \\","+  COUNTER(requested)                                                                               \\","+  GAUGE(active, Accumulate)                                                                        \\","+  GAUGE(pending, Accumulate)","+","+// Stats of the dynamic certificates, in the scope of the TLS context.","+struct DynamicCertificateStats {","+  ALL_DYNAMIC_CERTIFICATE_STATS(GENERATE_COUNTER_STRUCT, GENERATE_GAUGE_STRUCT)","+};","+"," /**","  * Selection handle of a dynamic certificate. It keeps the certificate alive for the handshake that","  * uses it, or holds